  "description": "Overview: Get ready to Code Today. Create Tomorrow! The Department of CSE (Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning), KPR Institute of Engineering and Technology, in association with the IEEE Computational Intelligence Society – KPRIET Student Branch, presents Hack The Horizon 2.0 – an intense 24-hour innovation hackathon. Hackathon: 24 & 25 September 2026 10:00 AM, 24 September – 10:00 AM, 25 September Venue: KPR Institute of Engineering and Technology Registration Fee: ₹700 per participant Team Size: 2–4 members Registration Deadline: Extended 15 September 2026, 11:59 PM For Registration : https://hack-the-horizon2.netlify.app/ Cash Prizes – ₹30,000: 1st Prize – ₹15,000 2nd Prize – ₹10,000 3rd Prize – ₹5,000 Participant Benefits: Event T-Shirt Complimentary food & refreshments throughout the hackathon Physical Certificate of Participation Important: Every team member must register and pay ₹700 individually. Team formation will be done through a separate form after registration closes. Bring your own laptop, charger, extension cord/power junction box, and other essentials. IoT/Hardware teams must bring all required components and hardware. College ID card is mandatory. Bring your idea. Build your solution. Make an impact! Register before 15 September 2026 and be part of Hack The Horizon 2.0!",
