    "details": "<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p>\n<p>Get ready to Code Today. Create Tomorrow!</p>\n<p>The Department of CSE (Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning), KPR Institute of Engineering and Technology, in association with the IEEE Computational Intelligence Society &ndash; KPRIET Student Branch, presents Hack The Horizon 2.0 &ndash; an intense 24-hour innovation hackathon.</p>\n<p><strong>Hackathon:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>24 &amp; 25 September 2026</li>\n<li>10:00 AM, 24 September &ndash; 10:00 AM, 25 September</li>\n<li>Venue: KPR Institute of Engineering and Technology</li>\n<li>Registration Fee: ₹700 per participant</li>\n<li>Team Size: 2&ndash;4 members</li>\n<li>Registration Deadline: Extended 15 September 2026, 11:59 PM&nbsp;</li>\n<li>For Registration : https://hack-the-horizon2.netlify.app/</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Cash Prizes &ndash; ₹30,000:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>1st Prize &ndash; ₹15,000</li>\n<li>2nd Prize &ndash; ₹10,000</li>\n<li>3rd Prize &ndash; ₹5,000</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Participant Benefits:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Event T-Shirt</li>\n<li>Complimentary food &amp; refreshments throughout the hackathon</li>\n<li>Physical Certificate of Participation</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Important:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Every team member must register and pay ₹700 individually.</li>\n<li>Team formation will be done through a separate form after registration closes.</li>\n<li>Bring your own laptop, charger, extension cord/power junction box, and other essentials.</li>\n<li>IoT/Hardware teams must bring all required components and hardware.</li>\n<li>College ID card is mandatory.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Bring your idea. Build your solution. Make an impact!</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Register before 15 September 2026 and be part of Hack The Horizon 2.0!</strong></p>",
    "end_date": "2026-09-15T12:00:00+05:30",
